  "body": "* Removes \"MQ\" (\"Media Queries\"?) from the foundational layer\n* Fixes the typography for \"Web IDL\"\n* Replaces \"NPAPI\" with \"Service Workers\" in the top layer\n\nCloses #4711.\n\n---\n\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Before\n<th>After\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/617481/80154454-9a126080-858d-11ea-8da1-73d4bb3b94fb.png\">\n<td><img src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/617481/80154533-c332f100-858d-11ea-8c70-383e04961020.png\">\n</table>\n\n---\n\nI'm happy to discuss further improvements to the diagram, as long as we don't take too long for what is essentially a joke. The main thing on my mind is I don't really know what the \"next to\" section is supposed to convey. Fetch seems more foundational than \"next to\". The explicit callouts of three image formats (but, e.g., no video formats) seems a bit strange. And giving \"Geo\" (presumably the geolocation API?) a place of prominence seems random.\n\nI might swap the position of XML and Fetch, remove Geo, and do... something... about the image formats.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5481/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 28, 2020, 4:55 PM UTC (ea6ee97)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5481/ae81398...ea6ee97/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 28, 2020, 4:55 PM UTC (ea6ee97)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5481/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 28, 2020, 4:55 PM UTC (ea6ee97)\">/browsers.html</a>  ( <a 